{"format":1,"key":"zone:undercity","path":"/lore/zone/undercity","name":"Undercity","kind":"zone","label":"Capital","zone":{"key":"undercity","name":"Undercity","path":"/lore/zone/undercity"},"levels":"","description":"Deep beneath the shattered ruins of Lordaeron's Capital City lies the Undercity, the dark stronghold of the Forsaken. Originally carved out of ancient…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:undercity","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Deep beneath the shattered ruins of Lordaeron's Capital City lies the Undercity, the dark stronghold of the Forsaken. Originally carved out of ancient royal crypts and dungeons by the Scourge, it was seized by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and remade into an impenetrable subterranean sanctuary. Today it serves as the seat of Forsaken power and the Horde's vital bastion in the northern Eastern Kingdoms.","Long before the plague swept Lordaeron, the catacombs, dungeons, and sewers beneath the palace were collectively known as the Undercity. It held the tombs of nobility, the kingdom's deepest prisons—where the former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer was once held before his escape—and the poorest denizens of the realm. When Arthas Menethil murdered King Terenas and laid waste to the capital in 20 ADP, the prince ordered his undead servants to excavate and expand the subterranean passages into a fortified seat of Scourge rule."],"hash":"57ce7b","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"b7b229a332","sec":41},"female-narrator":{"sha":"54db30f944","sec":59}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Undercity","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Undercity"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/npc/sylvanas-windrunner","n":"Sylvanas Windrunner","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/topic/forsaken","n":"Forsaken","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/zone/tirisfal","n":"Tirisfal Glades","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/ruinsoflordaeron","n":"Ruins of Lordaeron","k":"dungeon"},{"p":"/lore/topic/lordaeron","n":"Lordaeron","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/topic/scourge","n":"Scou